n of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=6 x - 15\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518849 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33305ca8-993e-5669-8cdd-29a0f53049bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=6 y - 16\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518851} {:answer/id #uuid "7388c931-8ed1-5910-a56f-bdb49b33f077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=2 - 6 x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518865} {:answer/id #uuid "a31737f2-3715-5ef0-836c-94646c00e4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=6 x - 12\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518879} {:answer/id #uuid "b199391b-d9e7-54a6-8a84-f61a6fee1d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=6 x - 22\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518883} {:answer/id #uuid "f0da208c-172f-56be-8f71-402de868d7d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=6 x + 2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b199391b-d9e7-54a6-8a84-f61a6fee1d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=6 x - 22\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518883} :answer-field/id #uuid "071fde19-c232-53cf-b8a7-e96d15627979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518838}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ed4f78d-95a2-5ea0-b370-b6d2838b98e8" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=1.$ Given that the point $P(2,1,-10)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=3 x$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(2,1,-10)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,1) & =3(2) \\\\ & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(2,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,1)}(x-(2)) \\\\ z-(-10) & =(6)(x-(2)) \\\\ z & =6 x - 22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,1,-10)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=6 x - 22\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cefab39-ceab-5bc8-b0a6-6589512c35f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518841} {:answer/id #uuid "2436b4d1-ecfb-59f4-aa6f-855069b04715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) - 11\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518845} {:answer/id #uuid "73e698a6-6d04-547c-9b5f-4ec276a6998c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=\\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) - 11\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518866} {:answer/id #uuid "db31537a-46f7-5cd1-b388-050def923915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ z=- \\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(y + \\pi\\right) - 11\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518894} {:answer/id #uuid "e9561cfc-93a7-5e03-aceb-2536b8187850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(x + 3\\right) - 1