9-2be0655df4f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518856} {:answer/id #uuid "9b744279-4786-539e-8b14-a0ac7dcaa614" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\pi \\\\ z=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518877} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ee9880-1460-507f-9f47-0b486e7219c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\pi \\\\ z=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518884} {:answer/id #uuid "f5691efd-ed01-5d63-8ae5-b7036767a2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ z=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(y - 2 \\pi\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518901} {:answer/id #uuid "f72a30b8-ab34-560b-a74a-809ba598eb19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\pi \\\\ z=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x + 3\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b744279-4786-539e-8b14-a0ac7dcaa614" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\pi \\\\ z=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518877} :answer-field/id #uuid "29c535fc-40c1-5c8a-8618-286ea91174e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518848}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "767e873f-9d5e-53b8-a351-ac97e9472597" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=2 \\pi.$ Given that the point $P(3,2 \\pi,12)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=2 \\pi.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(3,2 \\pi,12)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(3,2 \\pi)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(3,2 \\pi):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,2 \\pi) & =(2 \\pi)\\cos((3)(2 \\pi))+\\cos(2 \\pi) \\\\ & =(2 \\pi)(1)+(1) \\\\ & =1 + 2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(3,2 \\pi)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(3,2 \\pi)}(x-(3)) \\\\ z-(12) & =(1 + 2 \\pi)(x-(3)) \\\\ z & =x + 2 \\pi x - 6 \\pi + 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(3,2 \\pi,12)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\pi \\\\ z=x + 2 \\pi x - 6 \\pi + 9\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0105290b-487b-5f1f-9501-389134f1bca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=47 - 12 x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518834} {:answer/id #uuid "24236d83-648f-5a18-8541-22604f3bbde7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=36 - 12 x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518844} {:answer/id #uuid "35c8f4ef-206c-5e98-9de6-d1e85ff05749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ z=23 - 12 y\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518852} {:answer/id #uuid "7c507875-5c28-5dc9-abdd-490db8d5ac41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=12 x - 25\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518870} {:answer/id #uuid "a32be06c-26db-59ef-b8a7-ca9804b0b48f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=- 12 x - 25\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0105290b-487b-5f1f-9501-389134f1bca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=47 - 12 x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518834} :answer-field/id #uuid "abdaedd2-6bab-53dd-a839-adbeb7a2ebf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518882}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a82901d-0f58-5609-a6df-af791bb2eff0" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=1.$ Given that the point $P(3,1,11)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=- 4 x$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(3,1,11)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(3,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(3,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,1) & =-4(3) \\\\ & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(3,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(3,1)}(x-(3)) \\\\ z-(11) & =(-12)(x-(3)) \\\\ z & =47 - 12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(3,1,11)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=47 - 12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02deddff-9059-5e47-9c26-85eaba82b228" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=24 - 8 x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518835} {:answer/id #uuid "25dc159f-2b25-5616-b689-0949e232380b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=24 - 8 y\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518846} {:answer/id #uuid "4595568e-9c5b-5c6a-b50a-4e0976745cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=- 8 x - 8\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518855} {:answer/id #uuid "6e88bdab-5911-5cd6-bc3d-20f02fa8a250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=8 x + 24\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518862} {:answer/id #uuid "fb77957b-ee3e-5ce8-a221-053fc85456f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=- 8 x - 16\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4595568e-9c5b-5c6a-b50a-4e0976745cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=- 8 x - 8\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518855} :answer-field/id #uuid "684747ba-1690-52b7-9620-6795807308d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518861}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89f1d011-ec53-59f6-a20b-6cfabf7d7062" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,2,8)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=4 x$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(-2,2,8)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(-2,2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(-2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(-2,2) & =4(-2) \\\\ & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(-2,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(-2,2)}(x-(-2)) \\\\ z-(8) & =(-8)(x-(-2)) \\\\ z & =- 8 x - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,2,8)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=- 8 x - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c7e5bc6-3ce9-57cd-8b9a-0381a5d18474" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=\\left(1 + \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right) + 1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518857} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc60967-6d2e-50e4-905c-cc0feba54c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right) + 1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518869} {:answer/id #uuid "b83e21f4-a13c-53b2-ba45-018d690024c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + \\pi\\right) \\left(x + 2\\right) + 1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518886} {:answer/id #uuid "ba464102-0e5b-538a-a4e3-bb2541309ebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518887} {:answer/id #uuid "ddce3b25-0430-5dd6-aba0-6c7e60b0efe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + \\pi\\right) \\left(y + \\pi\\right) + 1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bc60967-6d2e-50e4-905c-cc0feba54c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right) + 1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518869} :answer-field/id #uuid "90d1f17b-d36e-5039-825e-87ba9664f7d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518875}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9f960064-2b69-5f34-81df-4eb442e3790b" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=- \\pi.$ Given that the point $P(2,- \\pi,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=- \\pi.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(2,- \\pi,1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,- \\pi)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(2,- \\pi):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,- \\pi) & =(- \\pi)\\cos((2)(- \\pi))+\\cos(- \\pi) \\\\ & =(- \\pi)(1.0)+(-1.0) \\\\ & =- 1.0 \\pi - 1.0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(2,- \\pi)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,- \\pi)}(x-(2)) \\\\ z-(1) & =(- \\pi - 1)(x-(2)) \\\\ z & =- \\pi x - x + 3 + 2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,- \\pi,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\pi x - x + 3 + 2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0835f080-946f-5479-8136-b72dc3e8f778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- 3 \\pi \\\\ z=\\left(1 + 3 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right) + 5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518839} {:answer/id #uuid "444a15db-f996-5afb-9dc1-b5dbd979fb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- 3 \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + 3 \\pi\\right) \\left(x + 2\\right) + 5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518854} {:answer/id #uuid "4f40d0bb-59df-580a-a14d-05979cea1db5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- 3 \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + 3 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518859} {:answer/id #uuid "72af88ff-dd4b-5f3c-afc6-b00d287c28b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- 3 \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + 3 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right) + 5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518864} {:answer/id #uuid "dec231d5-37ff-5962-8c0d-9ec7fcfab521" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + 3 \\pi\\right) \\left(y + 3 \\pi\\right) + 5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72af88ff-dd4b-5f3c-afc6-b00d287c28b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- 3 \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + 3 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 2\\right) + 5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518864} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aacdf6b-281e-509d-a99f-a31dc7bf0081" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518853}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d26e87a6-496d-5e71-aea4-0db8f9e8170f" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=- 3 \\pi.$ Given that the point $P(2,- 3 \\pi,5)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=- 3 \\pi.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(2,- 3 \\pi,5)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,- 3 \\pi)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(2,- 3 \\pi):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,- 3 \\pi) & =(- 3 \\pi)\\cos((2)(- 3 \\pi))+\\cos(- 3 \\pi) \\\\ & =(- 3 \\pi)(1.0)+(-1.0) \\\\ & =- 3.0 \\pi - 1.0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(2,- 3 \\pi)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,- 3 \\pi)}(x-(2)) \\\\ z-(5) & =(- 3 \\pi - 1)(x-(2)) \\\\ z & =- 3 \\pi x - x + 7 + 6 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,- 3 \\pi,5)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- 3 \\pi \\\\ z=- 3 \\pi x - x + 7 + 6 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}]}
